This work is a port of DDT's fixed-point Mandelbrot generator.

  Original work: mandel99 / mandelF18A
  Author:        DDT (0x444454)
  Source:        https://github.com/0x444454/mandel99
  See also:      https://github.com/0x444454/mandelbr8
  Licence:       Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)

  This port:     mandelCVB
  Author:        Troy Schrapel (visrealm)
  Source:        https://github.com/visrealm/mandelcvb
  Licence:       Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)

Changes made in this port
-------------------------

The original TI-99/4A TMS9900 assembly program has been ported to CVBasic, so
it builds for every CVBasic target with an F18A-compatible VDP rather than the
TI-99/4A alone. Specifically:

  * The host CPU side (F18A setup, GPU image upload, render loop, user input,
    text rendering) was reimplemented in CVBasic.
  * The F18A GPU code was kept as TMS9900 assembly and is otherwise
    unchanged; the shared VRAM addresses were relocated to suit the CVBasic
    host, and the framebuffer base moved from >0000 to >1000.
  * Text glyphs are read from CVBasic's character set in VRAM instead of the
    TI-99 console GROM font, which is not available on other targets.
  * Frame timing uses the CVBasic runtime's interrupt handler and frame
    counter instead of a custom VBlank hook.

